{
  "metadata": { "name": "Calibration", "language_info": { "name": "JavaScipt", "version": "8.0" } },
  "jsnbversion": "v0.1",
  "cells": [
    {
      "code": "# Voltrix Tests — `/options/calibration`\n\nFit SABR, SVI, Heston, and CEV parameters to market option prices.\nAfter calibration, use the recovered parameters to reconstruct the vol smile\nand price options with the calibrated surface.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<h1>Voltrix Tests — <code>/options/calibration</code></h1>\n<p>Fit SABR, SVI, Heston, and CEV parameters to market option prices. After calibration, use the recovered parameters to reconstruct the vol smile and price options with the calibrated surface.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "const BASE = 'http://localhost:8000/v2';\n\nasync function post(path, body) {\n  const res = await fetch(`${BASE}${path}`, {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify(body),\n  });\n  return res.json();\n}\n\nfunction fmt(n, d = 6) { return typeof n === 'number' ? n.toFixed(d) : n; }\nfunction fmtPct(n) { return typeof n === 'number' ? (n * 100).toFixed(4) + '%' : n; }",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n## Shared Market Setup\n\nAll calibration tests use these common inputs.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>Shared Market Setup</h2>\n<p>All calibration tests use these common inputs.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "//>html\n<div style='display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap'>\n  <label>Spot <input id='cal-spot' type='number' value='100' style='width:80px'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='cal-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.005' style='width:80px'></label>\n  <label>Div Yield <input id='cal-div' type='number' value='0.0' step='0.005' style='width:80px'></label>\n  <label>Settlement <input id='cal-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Day Count\n    <select id='cal-dc'>\n      <option value='ACT/365'>ACT/365</option>\n      <option value='ACT/360'>ACT/360</option>\n      <option value='30/360'>30/360</option>\n    </select>\n  </label>\n</div>",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "// Read shared market inputs — run this cell before any calibration section.\nwindow.CAL = {\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('cal-spot').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('cal-rate').value),\n  dividend_yield:  parseFloat(document.getElementById('cal-div').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('cal-settle').value,\n  day_count:       document.getElementById('cal-dc').value,\n};\nscrib.show('Market setup: S=' + CAL.spot + ', r=' + CAL.rate + ', q=' + CAL.dividend_yield + ', settle=' + CAL.settlement_date);",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n## 1. SABR Calibration\n\nEnter observed call prices across strikes, then calibrate SABR (α, ρ, ν) with fixed β.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>1. SABR Calibration</h2>\n<p>Enter observed call prices across strikes, then calibrate SABR (α, ρ, ν) with fixed β.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "//>html\n<div style='margin-bottom:12px'>\n  <label>Expiry <input id='sabr-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label style='margin-left:16px'>β (fixed) <input id='sabr-beta' type='number' value='0.5' step='0.1' min='0' max='1' style='width:60px'></label>\n</div>\n<table border='1' cellpadding='4' id='sabr-table'>\n  <thead><tr><th>Strike</th><th>Option Type</th><th>Market Price</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='sabr-k' value='85'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='sabr-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='sabr-p' value='17.2' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='sabr-k' value='90'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='sabr-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='sabr-p' value='13.5' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='sabr-k' value='95'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='sabr-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='sabr-p' value='10.1' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='sabr-k' value='100' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='sabr-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='sabr-p' value='7.2'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='sabr-k' value='105' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='sabr-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='sabr-p' value='4.9'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='sabr-k' value='110' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='sabr-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='sabr-p' value='3.1'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='sabr-k' value='115' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='sabr-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='sabr-p' value='1.8'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "const sabrExpiry = document.getElementById('sabr-expiry').value;\nconst sabrBeta   = parseFloat(document.getElementById('sabr-beta').value);\nconst sabrObs    = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#sabr-table tbody tr')).map(row => ({\n  option_type:  row.querySelector('.sabr-t').value,\n  strike:       parseFloat(row.querySelector('.sabr-k').value),\n  expiry_date:  sabrExpiry,\n  market_price: parseFloat(row.querySelector('.sabr-p').value),\n}));\n\nscrib.show('Calibrating SABR...');\nconst sabr = await post('/options/calibration/sabr', { ...CAL, beta: sabrBeta, observations: sabrObs });\n\nif (sabr.error) {\n  scrib.show('Error: ' + sabr.error.message);\n} else {\n  scrib.show('--- SABR Calibration Result ---');\n  scrib.show('α (alpha):   ' + fmt(sabr.alpha));\n  scrib.show('β (beta):    ' + fmt(sabr.beta));\n  scrib.show('ρ (rho):     ' + fmt(sabr.rho));\n  scrib.show('ν (nu):      ' + fmt(sabr.nu));\n  scrib.show('RMSE (vol):  ' + fmtPct(sabr.rmse) + ' (' + fmt(sabr.rmse, 8) + ')');\n  scrib.show('Observations used: ' + sabr.n_observations);\n  scrib.show('Converged:   ' + sabr.converged);\n  window.SABR_PARAMS = sabr;\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n### 1a. SABR Smile Reconstruction\n\nEvaluate the calibrated SABR smile across a range of strikes and compare to market prices.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h3>1a. SABR Smile Reconstruction</h3>\n<p>Evaluate the calibrated SABR smile across a range of strikes and compare to market prices.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "if (!window.SABR_PARAMS) { scrib.show('Run the SABR calibration cell first.'); }\nelse {\n  const p = SABR_PARAMS;\n  const expiry = document.getElementById('sabr-expiry').value;\n  const strikes = [80, 85, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 115, 120];\n\n  const smileVols = await Promise.all(strikes.map(K =>\n    post('/options/volatility', {\n      type: 'implied', vol_type: 'sabr',\n      spot: CAL.spot, strike: K, rate: CAL.rate,\n      dividend_yield: CAL.dividend_yield,\n      settlement_date: CAL.settlement_date,\n      expiry_date: expiry,\n      model_params: { alpha: p.alpha, beta: p.beta, rho: p.rho, nu: p.nu },\n    })\n  ));\n\n  scrib.show('--- SABR Smile (calibrated) ---');\n  scrib.show('Strike | SABR σ      | Model Type');\n  strikes.forEach((K, i) => {\n    const v = smileVols[i];\n    if (v.error) { scrib.show('  ' + K + '  | Error: ' + v.error.message); }\n    else scrib.show('  ' + String(K).padStart(3) + '  | ' + fmtPct(v.volatility) + '  | ' + v.vol_model);\n  });\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n### 1b. SABR → Pricing Round-Trip\n\nPrice options at each market strike using the calibrated SABR surface and compare to market prices.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h3>1b. SABR → Pricing Round-Trip</h3>\n<p>Price options at each market strike using the calibrated SABR surface and compare to market prices.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "if (!window.SABR_PARAMS) { scrib.show('Run the SABR calibration cell first.'); }\nelse {\n  const p = SABR_PARAMS;\n  const obs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#sabr-table tbody tr')).map(row => ({\n    option_type:  row.querySelector('.sabr-t').value,\n    strike:       parseFloat(row.querySelector('.sabr-k').value),\n    expiry_date:  document.getElementById('sabr-expiry').value,\n    market_price: parseFloat(row.querySelector('.sabr-p').value),\n  }));\n\n  const modelPrices = await Promise.all(obs.map(o =>\n    post('/options/price', {\n      model: 'black_scholes',\n      option_type: o.option_type,\n      spot: CAL.spot, strike: o.strike, rate: CAL.rate,\n      dividend_yield: CAL.dividend_yield,\n      settlement_date: CAL.settlement_date, expiry_date: o.expiry_date,\n      day_count: CAL.day_count,\n      volatility: {\n        surface_type: 'sabr',\n        other_params: { alpha: p.alpha, beta: p.beta, rho: p.rho, nu: p.nu },\n      },\n    })\n  ));\n\n  scrib.show('Strike | Mkt Price | SABR Price | Error');\n  obs.forEach((o, i) => {\n    const mp = modelPrices[i];\n    if (mp.error) { scrib.show('  ' + o.strike + ' | Error: ' + mp.error.message); return; }\n    const err = mp.price - o.market_price;\n    scrib.show(\n      '  ' + String(o.strike).padStart(3) +\n      '  | ' + fmt(o.market_price, 4).padStart(9) +\n      ' | ' + fmt(mp.price, 4).padStart(10) +\n      ' | ' + (err >= 0 ? '+' : '') + fmt(err, 4)\n    );\n  });\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n## 2. SVI Calibration\n\nFit Gatheral raw SVI (a, b, ρ, m, σ) to a set of market prices.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>2. SVI Calibration</h2>\n<p>Fit Gatheral raw SVI (a, b, ρ, m, σ) to a set of market prices.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "//>html\n<div style='margin-bottom:12px'>\n  <label>Expiry <input id='svi-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n</div>\n<table border='1' cellpadding='4' id='svi-table'>\n  <thead><tr><th>Strike</th><th>Option Type</th><th>Market Price</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='svi-k' value='80'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='svi-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='svi-p' value='21.8' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='svi-k' value='85'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='svi-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='svi-p' value='17.5' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='svi-k' value='90'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='svi-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='svi-p' value='13.6' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='svi-k' value='95'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='svi-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='svi-p' value='10.2' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='svi-k' value='100' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='svi-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='svi-p' value='7.3'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='svi-k' value='105' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='svi-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='svi-p' value='5.0'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='svi-k' value='110' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='svi-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='svi-p' value='3.2'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='svi-k' value='115' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='svi-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='svi-p' value='1.9'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "const sviExpiry = document.getElementById('svi-expiry').value;\nconst sviObs    = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#svi-table tbody tr')).map(row => ({\n  option_type:  row.querySelector('.svi-t').value,\n  strike:       parseFloat(row.querySelector('.svi-k').value),\n  expiry_date:  sviExpiry,\n  market_price: parseFloat(row.querySelector('.svi-p').value),\n}));\n\nscrib.show('Calibrating SVI...');\nconst svi = await post('/options/calibration/svi', { ...CAL, observations: sviObs });\n\nif (svi.error) {\n  scrib.show('Error: ' + svi.error.message);\n} else {\n  scrib.show('--- SVI Calibration Result ---');\n  scrib.show('a:           ' + fmt(svi.a));\n  scrib.show('b:           ' + fmt(svi.b));\n  scrib.show('ρ (rho):     ' + fmt(svi.rho));\n  scrib.show('m:           ' + fmt(svi.m));\n  scrib.show('σ (sigma):   ' + fmt(svi.sigma));\n  scrib.show('RMSE (vol):  ' + fmtPct(svi.rmse));\n  scrib.show('Observations used: ' + svi.n_observations);\n  scrib.show('Converged:   ' + svi.converged);\n  window.SVI_PARAMS = svi;\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n### 2a. SVI Smile Reconstruction\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h3>2a. SVI Smile Reconstruction</h3>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "if (!window.SVI_PARAMS) { scrib.show('Run the SVI calibration cell first.'); }\nelse {\n  const p = SVI_PARAMS;\n  const expiry = document.getElementById('svi-expiry').value;\n  const strikes = [75, 80, 85, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 115, 120, 125];\n\n  const smileVols = await Promise.all(strikes.map(K =>\n    post('/options/volatility', {\n      type: 'implied', vol_type: 'svi',\n      spot: CAL.spot, strike: K, rate: CAL.rate,\n      dividend_yield: CAL.dividend_yield,\n      settlement_date: CAL.settlement_date, expiry_date: expiry,\n      model_params: { a: p.a, b: p.b, rho: p.rho, m: p.m, sigma: p.sigma },\n    })\n  ));\n\n  scrib.show('--- SVI Smile (calibrated) ---');\n  scrib.show('Strike | SVI σ');\n  strikes.forEach((K, i) => {\n    const v = smileVols[i];\n    if (v.error) scrib.show('  ' + K + '  | Error: ' + v.error.message);\n    else scrib.show('  ' + String(K).padStart(3) + '  | ' + fmtPct(v.volatility));\n  });\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n## 3. Heston Calibration\n\nFit the 5 Heston parameters (v₀, κ, θ, σᵥ, ρ) directly to option prices.\nUse multiple expiries for a better-identified fit.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>3. Heston Calibration</h2>\n<p>Fit the 5 Heston parameters (v₀, κ, θ, σᵥ, ρ) directly to option prices. Use multiple expiries for a better-identified fit.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "//>html\n<table border='1' cellpadding='4' id='heston-table'>\n  <thead><tr><th>Strike</th><th>Expiry</th><th>Option Type</th><th>Market Price</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='90'  style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-01-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='13.0' step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='95'  style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-01-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='9.8'  step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='100' style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-01-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='7.0'  step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='105' style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-01-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='4.8'  step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='110' style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-01-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='3.1'  step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='90'  style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-10-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='15.5' step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='95'  style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-10-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='12.2' step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='100' style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-10-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='9.4'  step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='105' style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-10-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='7.0'  step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='h-k' value='110' style='width:55px'></td><td><input type='date' class='h-e' value='2027-10-01'></td><td><select class='h-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='h-p' value='5.1'  step='0.01' style='width:65px'></td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "const hestonObs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#heston-table tbody tr')).map(row => ({\n  option_type:  row.querySelector('.h-t').value,\n  strike:       parseFloat(row.querySelector('.h-k').value),\n  expiry_date:  row.querySelector('.h-e').value,\n  market_price: parseFloat(row.querySelector('.h-p').value),\n}));\n\nscrib.show('Calibrating Heston (this may take 10-30 seconds)...');\nconst heston = await post('/options/calibration/heston', { ...CAL, observations: hestonObs });\n\nif (heston.error) {\n  scrib.show('Error: ' + heston.error.message);\n} else {\n  scrib.show('--- Heston Calibration Result ---');\n  scrib.show('v₀   (initial var):  ' + fmt(heston.v0) + '  → initial vol ≈ ' + fmtPct(Math.sqrt(heston.v0)));\n  scrib.show('κ    (mean-rev spd): ' + fmt(heston.kappa));\n  scrib.show('θ    (long-run var): ' + fmt(heston.theta) + '  → long-run vol ≈ ' + fmtPct(Math.sqrt(heston.theta)));\n  scrib.show('σᵥ   (vol of vol):   ' + fmt(heston.sigma_v));\n  scrib.show('ρ    (correlation):  ' + fmt(heston.rho));\n  scrib.show('RMSE (price):        ' + fmt(heston.rmse, 4));\n  scrib.show('Feller condition:    ' + heston.feller_condition_satisfied + ' (2κθ ' + (heston.feller_condition_satisfied ? '>' : '≤') + ' σᵥ²)');\n  scrib.show('Observations used:   ' + heston.n_observations);\n  scrib.show('Converged:           ' + heston.converged);\n  window.HESTON_PARAMS = heston;\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n### 3a. Heston Pricing Round-Trip\n\nPrice the same options using the calibrated Heston model and check fit quality.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h3>3a. Heston Pricing Round-Trip</h3>\n<p>Price the same options using the calibrated Heston model and check fit quality.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "if (!window.HESTON_PARAMS) { scrib.show('Run the Heston calibration cell first.'); }\nelse {\n  const p = HESTON_PARAMS;\n  const obs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#heston-table tbody tr')).map(row => ({\n    option_type:  row.querySelector('.h-t').value,\n    strike:       parseFloat(row.querySelector('.h-k').value),\n    expiry_date:  row.querySelector('.h-e').value,\n    market_price: parseFloat(row.querySelector('.h-p').value),\n  }));\n\n  const modelPrices = await Promise.all(obs.map(o =>\n    post('/options/price', {\n      model: 'heston',\n      option_type: o.option_type,\n      spot: CAL.spot, strike: o.strike, rate: CAL.rate,\n      dividend_yield: CAL.dividend_yield,\n      settlement_date: CAL.settlement_date, expiry_date: o.expiry_date,\n      day_count: CAL.day_count,\n      volatility: {\n        surface_type: 'heston',\n        other_params: {\n          v0: p.v0, kappa: p.kappa, theta: p.theta, sigma_v: p.sigma_v, rho: p.rho,\n        },\n      },\n    })\n  ));\n\n  scrib.show('Strike | Expiry     | Mkt Price | Heston Price | Error');\n  obs.forEach((o, i) => {\n    const mp = modelPrices[i];\n    if (mp.error) { scrib.show('Error: ' + mp.error.message); return; }\n    const err = mp.price - o.market_price;\n    scrib.show(\n      '  ' + String(o.strike).padStart(3) +\n      '  | ' + o.expiry_date +\n      ' | ' + fmt(o.market_price, 3).padStart(9) +\n      ' | ' + fmt(mp.price, 3).padStart(12) +\n      ' | ' + (err >= 0 ? '+' : '') + fmt(err, 4)\n    );\n  });\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n## 4. CEV Calibration\n\nFit CEV (σ, β) using the Hagan-Woodward implied-vol approximation — no Monte Carlo.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>4. CEV Calibration</h2>\n<p>Fit CEV (σ, β) using the Hagan-Woodward implied-vol approximation — no Monte Carlo.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "//>html\n<div style='margin-bottom:12px'>\n  <label>Expiry <input id='cev-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n</div>\n<table border='1' cellpadding='4' id='cev-table'>\n  <thead><tr><th>Strike</th><th>Option Type</th><th>Market Price</th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='cev-k' value='85'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='cev-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='cev-p' value='16.8' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='cev-k' value='90'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='cev-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='cev-p' value='13.2' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='cev-k' value='95'  style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='cev-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='cev-p' value='10.0' step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='cev-k' value='100' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='cev-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='cev-p' value='7.2'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='cev-k' value='105' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='cev-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='cev-p' value='4.9'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n    <tr><td><input type='number' class='cev-k' value='110' style='width:60px'></td><td><select class='cev-t'><option>call</option><option>put</option></select></td><td><input type='number' class='cev-p' value='3.1'  step='0.01' style='width:70px'></td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "const cevExpiry = document.getElementById('cev-expiry').value;\nconst cevObs    = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#cev-table tbody tr')).map(row => ({\n  option_type:  row.querySelector('.cev-t').value,\n  strike:       parseFloat(row.querySelector('.cev-k').value),\n  expiry_date:  cevExpiry,\n  market_price: parseFloat(row.querySelector('.cev-p').value),\n}));\n\nscrib.show('Calibrating CEV...');\nconst cev = await post('/options/calibration/cev', { ...CAL, observations: cevObs });\n\nif (cev.error) {\n  scrib.show('Error: ' + cev.error.message);\n} else {\n  scrib.show('--- CEV Calibration Result ---');\n  scrib.show('σ (sigma):   ' + fmt(cev.sigma));\n  scrib.show('β (beta):    ' + fmt(cev.beta) + '  (1=log-normal, 0=normal)');\n  scrib.show('RMSE (vol):  ' + fmtPct(cev.rmse));\n  scrib.show('Observations used: ' + cev.n_observations);\n  scrib.show('Converged:   ' + cev.converged);\n  window.CEV_PARAMS = cev;\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n### 4a. CEV Vol Smile via /options/volatility\n\nUse the calibrated CEV params with the `cev` vol_type to get BS-equivalent vols across strikes.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h3>4a. CEV Vol Smile via /options/volatility</h3>\n<p>Use the calibrated CEV params with the <code>cev</code> vol_type to get BS-equivalent vols across strikes.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "if (!window.CEV_PARAMS) { scrib.show('Run the CEV calibration cell first.'); }\nelse {\n  const p = CEV_PARAMS;\n  const expiry = document.getElementById('cev-expiry').value;\n  const strikes = [80, 85, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 115, 120];\n\n  const vols = await Promise.all(strikes.map(K =>\n    post('/options/volatility', {\n      type: 'implied', vol_type: 'cev',\n      spot: CAL.spot, strike: K, rate: CAL.rate,\n      dividend_yield: CAL.dividend_yield,\n      settlement_date: CAL.settlement_date, expiry_date: expiry,\n      model_params: { sigma: p.sigma, beta: p.beta },\n    })\n  ));\n\n  scrib.show('--- CEV Implied Vol Smile ---');\n  scrib.show('Strike | CEV-equiv σ');\n  strikes.forEach((K, i) => {\n    const v = vols[i];\n    if (v.error) scrib.show('  ' + K + '  | Error');\n    else scrib.show('  ' + String(K).padStart(3) + '  | ' + fmtPct(v.volatility));\n  });\n}",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n## 5. Model Comparison\n\nCalibrate all models to the same market prices and compare RMSE.\nUses the prices from section 1 (SABR table). Run sections 1 and 2 first.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>5. Model Comparison</h2>\n<p>Calibrate all models to the same market prices and compare RMSE. Uses the prices from section 1 (SABR table). Run sections 1 and 2 first.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "const compObs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#sabr-table tbody tr')).map(row => ({\n  option_type:  row.querySelector('.sabr-t').value,\n  strike:       parseFloat(row.querySelector('.sabr-k').value),\n  expiry_date:  document.getElementById('sabr-expiry').value,\n  market_price: parseFloat(row.querySelector('.sabr-p').value),\n}));\n\nscrib.show('Running all calibrations for comparison...');\nconst [sabrComp, sviComp, cevComp] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/calibration/sabr', { ...CAL, beta: 0.5, observations: compObs }),\n  post('/options/calibration/svi',  { ...CAL, observations: compObs }),\n  post('/options/calibration/cev',  { ...CAL, observations: compObs }),\n]);\n\nscrib.show('--- Model Fit Comparison (same market prices) ---');\nscrib.show('Model  | RMSE (vol)    | Converged | # Params');\nscrib.show('SABR   | ' + (sabrComp.rmse ? fmtPct(sabrComp.rmse) : 'error').padEnd(13) + ' | ' + String(sabrComp.converged).padEnd(9) + ' | 3 (α,ρ,ν) + fixed β');\nscrib.show('SVI    | ' + (sviComp.rmse  ? fmtPct(sviComp.rmse)  : 'error').padEnd(13) + ' | ' + String(sviComp.converged).padEnd(9)  + ' | 5 (a,b,ρ,m,σ)');\nscrib.show('CEV    | ' + (cevComp.rmse  ? fmtPct(cevComp.rmse)  : 'error').padEnd(13) + ' | ' + String(cevComp.converged).padEnd(9)  + ' | 2 (σ,β)');",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n## 6. Synthetic Round-Trip Test (SABR)\n\nGenerate synthetic market prices from known SABR parameters, calibrate back,\nand verify the recovered parameters match the inputs.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>6. Synthetic Round-Trip Test (SABR)</h2>\n<p>Generate synthetic market prices from known SABR parameters, calibrate back, and verify the recovered parameters match the inputs.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "//>html\n<div style='display:flex;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap'>\n  <label>True α <input id='rt-alpha' type='number' value='0.3'  step='0.05' style='width:60px'></label>\n  <label>True β <input id='rt-beta2' type='number' value='0.5'  step='0.1'  min='0' max='1' style='width:60px'></label>\n  <label>True ρ <input id='rt-rho'   type='number' value='-0.4' step='0.1'  style='width:60px'></label>\n  <label>True ν <input id='rt-nu'    type='number' value='0.6'  step='0.1'  style='width:60px'></label>\n  <label>Expiry <input id='rt-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n</div>",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "const trueAlpha  = parseFloat(document.getElementById('rt-alpha').value);\nconst trueBeta   = parseFloat(document.getElementById('rt-beta2').value);\nconst trueRho    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('rt-rho').value);\nconst trueNu     = parseFloat(document.getElementById('rt-nu').value);\nconst rtExpiry   = document.getElementById('rt-expiry').value;\n\nconst rtStrikes = [85, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 115];\n\n// Step 1: generate prices using the known SABR surface\nconst rtPrices = await Promise.all(rtStrikes.map(K =>\n  post('/options/price', {\n    model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call',\n    spot: CAL.spot, strike: K, rate: CAL.rate,\n    dividend_yield: CAL.dividend_yield,\n    settlement_date: CAL.settlement_date, expiry_date: rtExpiry,\n    day_count: CAL.day_count,\n    volatility: {\n      surface_type: 'sabr',\n      other_params: { alpha: trueAlpha, beta: trueBeta, rho: trueRho, nu: trueNu },\n    },\n  })\n));\n\nconst rtObs = rtStrikes.map((K, i) => ({\n  option_type: 'call', strike: K,\n  expiry_date: rtExpiry,\n  market_price: rtPrices[i].price,\n}));\n\n// Step 2: calibrate back\nconst rtResult = await post('/options/calibration/sabr', { ...CAL, beta: trueBeta, observations: rtObs });\n\nscrib.show('--- SABR Synthetic Round-Trip ---');\nscrib.show('Param | Input  | Recovered | Error');\nscrib.show('α     | ' + trueAlpha.toFixed(4) + ' | ' + fmt(rtResult.alpha, 4) + '    | ' + fmt(Math.abs(rtResult.alpha - trueAlpha), 6));\nscrib.show('ρ     | ' + trueRho.toFixed(4)   + ' | ' + fmt(rtResult.rho, 4)   + '    | ' + fmt(Math.abs(rtResult.rho   - trueRho),   6));\nscrib.show('ν     | ' + trueNu.toFixed(4)    + ' | ' + fmt(rtResult.nu, 4)    + '    | ' + fmt(Math.abs(rtResult.nu    - trueNu),    6));\nscrib.show('RMSE (vol): ' + (rtResult.rmse ? rtResult.rmse.toExponential(3) : 'n/a'));\nscrib.show('Converged: ' + rtResult.converged);",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    },
    {
      "code": "---\n\n## 7. Error Handling\n\nTest that the API returns clear errors for invalid inputs.\n",
      "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>7. Error Handling</h2>\n<p>Test that the API returns clear errors for invalid inputs.</p>\n", "type": "html"
    },
    {
      "code": "// Too few observations\nconst err1 = await post('/options/calibration/heston', {\n  ...CAL,\n  observations: [\n    { option_type: 'call', strike: 100, expiry_date: '2027-04-01', market_price: 7.0 },\n    { option_type: 'call', strike: 105, expiry_date: '2027-04-01', market_price: 4.5 },\n  ],\n});\nscrib.show('Too few observations → ' + (err1.error ? err1.error.code + ': ' + err1.error.message : 'no error (unexpected)'));\n\n// Expiry before settlement\nconst err2 = await post('/options/calibration/sabr', {\n  ...CAL,\n  beta: 0.5,\n  observations: [\n    { option_type: 'call', strike: 100, expiry_date: '2025-01-01', market_price: 5.0 },\n  ],\n});\nscrib.show('Expiry before settlement → ' + (err2.error ? err2.error.code + ': ' + err2.error.message : 'no error (unexpected)'));\n\n// Missing model_params for parametric vol_type\nconst err3 = await post('/options/volatility', {\n  type: 'implied', vol_type: 'sabr',\n  spot: 100, strike: 100, rate: 0.05,\n  settlement_date: CAL.settlement_date, expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n});\nscrib.show('Missing model_params → ' + (err3.error ? err3.error.code + ': ' + err3.error.message : 'no error (unexpected)'));",
      "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code"
    }
  ],
  "source": "https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/scribbler",
  "run_on_load": false
